# Firmware configuration headers

`device_config.h` defines the only accepted local configuration record: Wi-Fi,
provisioned device ID/secret, HTTPS backend origin and issuing root CA. The
record is fixed-size, versioned, checksummed, validated before use, and stored
in NVS by `recovery_portal.cpp`; no credential is compiled into the firmware.

Fleet confidentiality depends on the `esp32dev-secure` flash/NVS encryption
gate. See `../README.md`,
`../../hardware/HARDWARE_TELEMETRY.md`, and
`../../operations/HARDWARE_SECURITY_PROVISIONING.md` for provisioning,
rotation, key custody, and physical acceptance.
